				"16:9, 5 seconds, ultra cinematic photoreal, one continuous \ntake, aggressive speed ramping, hyper-stylized.\n\nScene: A black void. A single glowing orb of liquid light \nfloats in darkness, pulsing like a heartbeat. Suddenly the \norb explodes into a torrent of golden particles racing \nthrough the void.\n\n0-1s — Crash Zoom In:\nCamera rockets toward the orb at bullet velocity. Hard freeze \n3 inches from the surface. The orb's surface ripples like mercury, \nreflecting infinite fractals of light.\n\n1-2s — Explosion:\nThe orb shatters in extreme slow motion. Golden shards and \nliquid light burst outward in all directions. Time freezes \nmid-explosion, debris hanging in the air like a sculpture.\n\n2-3.5s — Whip Through Chaos:\nCamera punches forward through the frozen explosion, weaving \nbetween shards at impossible speed, motion blur streaks. \nEmerges into a vast cathedral of floating geometric structures—\nglowing nodes connected by streams of pure light, like a \nliving neural network in deep space.\n\n3.5-5s — Final Reveal:\nCamera pulls back explosively. The neural network compresses \ninto a single radiant symbol at the center of frame. Volumetric \nlight beams pierce outward. Hard cut to black.\n\nStyle: Marvel opening titles meets Apple keynote, \nDune-level scale, hyperreal materials, lens flare, \ndeep blacks with electric gold and cyan accents, \ncrystalline detail, IMAX cinematography.\n\nAudio: Deep sub-bass build, glass shatter on freeze, \nsynth riser through the whip, thunderous bass drop on reveal, \nsilence on cut to black.",
